sonora (0.3.6) unstable; urgency=low

  * Fix: a playlist that contains only a .cue file (no separate FLAC entry)
    hung when a track was started: the player waited for ASYNC_DONE, which
    playbin does not deliver to a polling application. The file is now
    opened in PAUSED and the pre-roll is polled, then the track is sought.
  * Fix: tracks of a cue sheet end with EOS at the right position (SEGMENT_DONE
    is never delivered); the stop position is always set, so the last track
    no longer ends immediately; same fix for resuming after a sound-service
    change.
  * Safety: playback stops when 8 tracks end within a second; open timeout.
  * Cue sheets with full Windows paths are resolved by file name.
  * SONORA_DEBUG=1 prints player events (open, pre-roll, seek, EOS, errors).

 -- Your Name <you@example.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0100

sonora (0.3.5) unstable; urgency=low

  * CUE sheet support: a .cue (with FLAC/APE/WV/WAV/MP3 ... image) is expanded
    into one playlist entry per track, with title/artist/album/year/genre from
    the sheet; folders skip audio files that a cue sheet already covers.
  * Player: playing a part of a file, tracks of one image switch without
    re-opening the file; time and seeking are relative to the track.

 -- Your Name <you@example.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

